; Checkpoints: room, row and column of the 10 places the monk restarts at
;
; Ten records of 3 bytes read by #R$BDF3: +0 byte room number, +1 byte row (character rows, 0-21), +2 byte column
; (0-31). The monk restarts there with y = row * 4 and x = column * 4 in 2-pixel units, in character cells. Records 1
; to 9 belong to the nine checkpoint flags at #R$8543 in the same order (the checkpoint items of rooms 7, 8, 11, 12,
; 14, 15, 19, 21 and 23, #R$8FFF to #R$903F); the tenth is used while no checkpoint has been touched: the start of the
; game in room 5. Room names: 7 Abandoned church, 8 The Altar, 11 Cave of illusions, 12 Plagued ruins, 14 Hidden
; garden, 15 Gloomy tunels, 19 Underground river, 21 Evil church, 23 Ashes to ashes, 5 Escape !!!.
@label=Checkpoints
b$BE2A DEFB $07,$10,$02 ; flag 1: Abandoned church
 $BE2D DEFB $08,$11,$07 ; flag 2: The Altar
 $BE30 DEFB $0B,$11,$0E ; flag 3: Cave of illusions
 $BE33 DEFB $0C,$07,$08 ; flag 4: Plagued ruins
 $BE36 DEFB $0E,$11,$08 ; flag 5: Hidden garden
 $BE39 DEFB $0F,$07,$15 ; flag 6: Gloomy tunels
 $BE3C DEFB $13,$0B,$08 ; flag 7: Underground river
 $BE3F DEFB $15,$05,$13 ; flag 8: Evil church
 $BE42 DEFB $17,$11,$11 ; flag 9: Ashes to ashes
 $BE45 DEFB $05,$11,$09 ; none touched: Escape !!!, the start
